<!-- AREAS -->
<section style="padding:76px 24px 60px;background:#fff;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">
    <span class="kicker">Service Areas</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,36px);margin:0 0 16px;">Serving Calgary</h2>
    <div class="rich" style="text-align:left;"><p>Independent builders quoting through this site work in Calgary and the surrounding towns, and each town has its own permit office and rules. See <a href='/garage-builders-airdrie/'>garage builders in Airdrie</a>, <a href='/garage-builders-cochrane/'>Cochrane</a>, <a href='/garage-builders-okotoks/'>Okotoks</a>, <a href='/garage-builders-chestermere/'>Chestermere</a> and <a href='/garage-builders-rocky-view-county/'>Rocky View County</a>, or stay on the Calgary pages if your lot is inside the city.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#F3F2EE;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">How do garage prices and scoping work?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Each independent builder sets its own price; this site does not quote. Calgary builders advertise package starting prices, for example Corsac Construction lists a 22' x 22' double at $27,500 plus GST and Venkor Group lists a 22 x 22 double at $30126, while Precision Construction & Decora describes a finished double at $55,000 to $90,000. Package inclusions differ, so ask each builder to write down the size, slab, framing, door, electrical and whether permits are in the price.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">How quickly will a builder respond, and how long does a build take?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">This site does not guarantee a response time, because each builder keeps its own schedule. Ask when the written proposal will arrive and when work could start. The City of Calgary says a building permit review takes approximately 7 days, or 10 to 12 weeks if a development permit is needed, and that neither is guaranteed. Sahi Contracting says most builds take 3 to 5 weeks once permits are in hand, while Falcon Contracting says 4 to 8 weeks from excavation to inspection.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">Do I need a permit for a detached garage in Calgary?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">The City of Calgary says a detached garage over 10 square metres (107 sq. ft.) needs a building permit, and a separate electrical permit for lights and the door opener. A development permit is also needed in some cases, for example a garage over 75 square metres (807 sq. ft.) or higher than 4.6 metres. Confirm your lot with the City before you commit to a design.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">Is Back Lane Garage Co a garage builder?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">No. It advertises independent garage builders and does not build, employ crews, pull permits or hold a contracting licence. A builder that accepts deposits or progress payments from homeowners before the work is finished may need a provincial licence. Service Alberta has a search where you can check whether a business is licensed.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">Can a garage be built in winter?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Some builders say yes. Falcon Contracting says winter builds are possible with specialized concrete techniques and may cost slightly more for heating, and Hammerhead Construction says concrete needs winter heat to pour. Hammerhead also notes that more projects are completed in summer, so demand for labour can be higher. Asking for quotes in winter gives you time to plan a spring or summer build.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">Do the rules differ outside Calgary?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Yes. Airdrie, Cochrane, Okotoks, Chestermere and Rocky View County each publish their own permit rules, fees and setbacks, and some of those details differ from the City of Calgary's. Start with the page for your town and confirm the current rules with the municipality before you sign anything.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

